/-
# Auxiliary lemmas for the functional `ω` of the assembly of `coker_obstruction`

`ω` is defined by the sum of the local pairings of the data `(α, β)` against `b₀ ∘ res k N`, where
`b₀` is a `1`-cocycle `Gal(N/k) → E^∨(1)`.  Two local constancy facts are needed (the pairing is
only defined on locally constant cochains):

* `isLocConstOn_comp_res`: any `b₀ ∘ res k N` is locally constant (take the open subgroup
  `N.fixingSubgroup = ker (res k N)`);
* `isLocConstOn_zpowers_of_sq_eq_one`: for `c ^ 2 = 1` every function is locally constant on
  `zpowers c` (the subgroup is `{1, c}` and the Krull topology separates `c` from `1`).
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.Interfaces
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.DualMod.Main
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.ShaCocycles
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.H1Pair.Pairing
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.H1Pair.DualRestrict
import Submission.Work.SSGRoute.H1Pair.Clauses
